Recorded pages of ollama.com, fetched once on 2026-11-21 with the user agent of the add-on:
  search-qwen.html   GET /search?q=qwen&o=popular&c=tools (the site redirects to /search?c=tools&q=qwen)
  search-empty.html  GET /search?c=local&q=zzqxjkvv (a page with no results)
  tags-qwen3.html    GET /library/qwen3/tags
  tags-q38.html      GET /library/qwen3.8/tags (tags of MLX, nvfp4 and mxfp8 builds next to GGUF ones)
The tests read these files and never call the live site. Record them again, by hand and
politely, when the site changes its markup.
The search page lists the first 14 of the results it counts (data-result-count is the
total, data-has-more is true) and loads the rest with a script, so one request gives at
most about 14 rows.
